	(text_box "POWER / PCB\nJ1.11/12 -> VSYS (module VBAT: 2.9-5.5V).\nJ1.15/16 -> SYS_3V3 (3.15-3.45V).\nJ1.2/8/13/14/21 -> GND; 9/10 explicitly NC.\nInternal IC passives are not duplicated.\nRoute both VBAT pins and every GND pin.\n02_POWER rails are local labels: export them\nin the later integration pass to power this sheet.\nNo PWR_FLAG hides the missing source."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 113.03 0)
		(size 83.82 30.48)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "19b88294-538d-56cb-ac0a-9d3510916160")
	)
	(text_box "CONNECTOR / ASSEMBLY\nOK-23GF024-04 socket mates with module's OK-23GM024-04 male (module P5, OCN P1/P3).\nFootprint F.Cu view: lower row 1..12 left-to-right; upper row 24..13 left-to-right.\nPin 1 is marked at lower left. Mating-face views reflect across the connector long axis.\nMatch to P5 FPC pin-1 corner; check folded FPC orientation before board placement."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 115.57 0)
		(size 78.74 27.94)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "349c6e32-0f06-5b1d-93e3-010d37684e2c")
	)
	(text_box "Pin 16 documentation discrepancy: mechanical drawing P5 labels VDD; interface table P9 labels TP_VDD. Both require 3.3 V in this design. P9 naming used pending supplier clarification."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 96.52 31.75 0)
		(size 162.56 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "547ffe65-1b09-54b8-8399-6b7dea98287f")
	)
	(text_box "ZC-A1D43W-046  |  466 x 466 AMOLED + touch\nJ1 = motherboard socket. Display/touch/power ICs are inside the module.\nPhysical buttons remain the primary sports controls; touch is an additional UI input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 12.7 0)
		(size 254 11.43)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b195876-2ee3-5f4c-bc65-a249267b2f81")
	)
	(text_box "TOUCH I2C — R301 / R302 DNP\n3.6k provisions to SYS_3V3; fit only if needed.\nProvisional target: 100kHz, total Cbus <=100pF.\nNXP UM10204 calculation: 0.967k < Rp < 11.8k.\nCHSC datasheets specify no resistor value.\nConfirm module pull-ups, sink capability and\nfinal bus capacitance before population.\nDo not use 1.8V PMIC bus pull-ups."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 81.28 0)
		(size 78.74 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b528fdc4-f279-53c7-84ff-9ae8e83d11a4")
	)
	(text_box "HOST DEFAULT STATES\nR303/R304 = 100k reset pull-downs.\nAt 3.3V: ~33uA each while reset is driven high.\nR303: CO5300 input leakage <=1uA; 100k is safe.\nR304: CHSC6417 reset leakage unspecified; verify bring-up.\nR305 = 10k QSPI CS pull-up.\nR306 DNP until VCI_EN bias/polarity is confirmed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 119.38 0)
		(size 78.74 24.13)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c7a5f61a-222b-53ea-a0f1-f9d1686c4fbe")
	)
	(text_box "FIRMWARE / INTEGRATION — Apollo balls unallocated; all interfaces are 3.3V\nCO5300 pp100/101/116: hold DISP_RST low at startup; VDDI must precede internal VCI.\nWait >=10ms after rails valid before releasing reset; >=10ms before first command;\nwait >=120ms after reset before Sleep Out, then >=60ms before Display On.\nShutdown: Display Off -> Sleep In -> wait >=83ms -> reset low -> internal VCI off before VDDI.\nVCI_EN controls internal power: obtain module enable polarity/delays and initialization code.\nCHSC6417 section 8: TOUCH_RST low >=100us before power; hold >=1ms after power valid;\nreset pulse >=500us; allow up to 200ms for ready INT. Power cycle: <0.3V for >=2ms.\nTP_VDD rise (10-90%) <=5ms; assert TOUCH_RST before power-down.\nKeep shared I2C idle during touch reset; never drive it while TP_VDD is off.\nModule timing and internal bias must be confirmed on hardware before production release."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 149.86 0)
		(size 154.94 35.56)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c86ba6c1-cbd6-5c5a-af04-fc193c8f0e6c")
	)
